In Mail subject FIRING:
The numbers [FIRING:7] and [FIRING:4] are not alert severities or "remaining alerts." They indicate how many alerts Alertmanager grouped into a single email.

From your screenshot:

[FIRING:7] kube-system
There are 7 firing alerts in the kube-system namespace.
These are likely default Kubernetes alerts from kube-prometheus-stack (for example, Watchdog, KubeSchedulerDown, KubeProxyDown, etc.).
[FIRING:4] logapp
There are 4 firing alerts related to your logapp.
Since your alert expressions are evaluated per pod, if you have multiple pods and multiple rules, Alertmanager groups them.

For example, suppose you have:

3 pods
3 custom rules:
PredictionRequestsZero
NoFileUploads
TooManyFailures

If two rules are firing on two pods, Alertmanager may group them into one email.
